ntime DB numbers) are invisible, so an unreachable block is a candidate, not proof. Not live-tested. External sources, folders and devices (not live-tested): list_external_sources (optional plcName; the external sources of each PLC and of its software units, by name; groups inside the External source files folder are not supported by Openness and not listed), read_tag_comments (optional plcName, tableName, folderPath; the multilingual comment of every tag and user constant, one {culture, text} entry per language with a text), find_objects (pattern with * and ?, matched case-insensitively against the whole name; optional plcName, kinds, offset, limit 1-1000; software units, blocks, block groups, PLC data types and their groups, tag tables and their folders, tags and user constants of the PLC's own tag tables, watch tables, force tables and their groups, external sources, from the project tree, list_tag_tables, list_watch_and_force_tables and list_external_sources; sorted, paged, with totalMatches, nextOffset and complete; technology objects are not searched) and scan_accessible_devices (mode and pcInterface { name, number } as get_online_state lists them, both required, no default; optional plcName and maxElements 1-1000; ConfigurationPcInterface.GetAccessibleDevices() performs live network discovery through that one interface and changes nothing, allowed in every mode like compare_to_online (the access mode is the only control; the caller names the interface); TIA Portal dialogs during the scan are answered No and fail the item; each device reports name, deviceSeries, address and macAddress). Alarms and text lists (not live-tested): list_text_lists (optional plcName, omitted reads every PLC; projectLanguages { active, editing, reference } and per PLC the user and system text lists with name, isSystem, id, listRange and comment per culture; text list entries are not part of the documented object model), read_text_list_workbook (optional plcName, textListNames, cultures, maxElements, sheet, startRow, startColumn), read_alarm_text_workbook (exportOption, a PlcAlarmTextXlsxExportOption member; optional plcName, cultures, maxElements, sheet, startRow, startColumn) and read_supervision_workbook (blockPath of a ProDiag FB, optional maxElements, sheet, startRow, startColumn): TIA Portal's XLSX export into a temporary file that is deleted again (every TIA Portal dialog during it is answered No and fails the read), returned as uninterpreted cells { sheets[{ name, rowCount, columnCount, cellCount, rows[{ row, cells[{ cell, kind, value, valueTruncated }], cellsTruncated, nextStartColumn }], rowsTruncated, nextStartRow }], workbookHash } (the column layout is TIA Portal's; at most maxElements rows per sheet, default 50, and never more than the value budget, which several workbook reads of one call share: page on with sheet and startRow = nextStartRow, and a row cut at the budget with startRow = that row and startColumn = nextStartColumn; workbookHash covers every cell and is the expectedWorkbookHash of plc_write update_*_cells). get_prodiag_fb (blockPath: ProgrammingLanguage, isProDiag, FB.Supervisions.Count, IsConsistent and the ProDiagVersion, InitialValueAcquisition, UseCentralTimeStamp attributes) and get_prodiag_assignment (AssignedProDiagFB of a tag: tableName and name, optional folderPath and plcName; or of an instance DB or global DB member: blockPath, optional memberPath). Technology objects (PlcSoftware.TechnologicalObjectGroup; not live-tested): list_technology_objects (optional plcName; optional folderPath narrows one PLC to a group subtree; objects with name, groupPath, number, systemLibElement and systemLibVersion (OfSystemLibElement/OfSystemLibVersion), runtimeType, and the user groups), get_technology_object_parameters (name; optional prefix, offset and limit 1-2000 default 200 with nextOffset, or parameterName for one exact Find; every value is typed by its runtime type: valueKind boolean|integer|real|string|enum|plcTag|null|object|unreadable, valueType, value as invariant text and enumMembers), get_technology_object_hardware_connection (name; every documented provider the object lists among its services: actor, sensor and torque (axis), sensor (encoder), measuringInput, outputCam, ident, with isConnected and the documented properties, connected modules as modulePath) and get_technology_object_content (name; SimaticML with contentHash for update_technology_object_content). Fail-safe (F-) PLCs (not live-tested; every Siemens.Engineering.Safety member is bound at runtime by exact name, a missing one is reported api_member_missing): get_safety_administration (optional plcName, omitted reads every PLC; per PLC whether its CPU offers SafetyAdministration, passwordSet (IsSafetyOfflineProgramPasswordSet), loggedOn (IsLoggedOnToSafetyOfflineProgram), the SafetySettings values (SafetySystemVersion, applicable versions, F-change history, block number ranges), every F-runtime group with its attributes (main safety block and IDB, F-OB, cycle times) and attributeInfos (every attribute GetAttributeInfos lists, with its access mode, to see what is writable), the collective program signatures, the Safety services the CPU lists and the safety unit names; plus TIA Portal's GlobalSettings getters such as SafetyModificationsPossible) and list_safety_blocks (optional plcName, offset, limit 1-2000 default 200; every block that offers SafetySignatureProvider or has an F_ language, with its signatures). Reads change nothing and are no safety acceptance evidence. Offline change detection (issue #6; not live-tested; every member is bound at runtime): get_plc_checksums (optional plcName, omitted reads every PLC; per PLC whether its PlcSoftware lists and returns Siemens.Engineering.SW.PlcChecksumProvider among GetServiceInfos(), and its Software and TextLists checksums projected as text { state value|empty|null|unreadable|missing, value, runtimeType, error } because the reference gives no type; empty or null means, per the Siemens change-detection skill, not compiled or changed since the last compile) and get_fingerprints (exactly one of blockPath or typePath; FingerprintProvider.GetFingerprints() of that block or PLC data type, found among its GetServiceInfos() (not listed: unsupported_capability; GetFingerprints missing: api_member_missing), every Fingerprint's Id and Value as text in the same shape). The online FingerprintDataProvider is not offered. Project languages (issue #8, not live-tested): get_project_languages (no fields; project-wide: LanguageSettings.ActiveLanguages, EditingLanguage and ReferenceLanguage as culture names, every supported language of LanguageSettings.Languages, and the text categories { identifier, name } of ProjectBase.TextCategories that export_project_texts takes). Block protection (issue #5, not live-tested): get_block_protection (blockPath; the block's PlcBlock.IsKnowHowProtected, programming language and isFailSafe, and for PlcBlockProtectionProvider (know-how) and PlcBlockWriteProtectionProvider (IsDefined, IsProtected) whether the block's GetServiceInfos() lists and returns them, which documented members bind and the characters GetInvalidPasswordCharacters() returns; an unreadable value is null with a note). OPC UA (issue #24; not live-tested; members bound at runtime): get_opcua_configuration (optional plcName, omitted reads every PLC; from the PlcSoftware's OpcUaProvider service (not listed: providerAvailable false with a note): the server interfaces (companion specifications and own interfaces), SIMATIC interfaces and reference namespaces with name, enabled, author, comment, creationTime, lastModified, useStringNodeIds, generateNodes, generatedInterfaceName, and the access control: namespace access restrictions (namespaceUri, namespaceIndex, sessionRequired, signingRequired, encryptionRequired, applyRestrictionsToBrowse) and role mappings (name, definedInNamespace, projectRole, roleId, namespacePermissions with browse, read, write, call, receiveEvents, readRolePermissions)). Reads run independently, so a failing item does not stop later operations. Content results are { format, content, contentHash, warnings }; contentHash is null for withDependencies reads. list_tag_tables returns { isComplete, messages, plcs[] } and list_download_targets returns { plcs[{ plcName, deviceName, downloadable, modes[] }] } as declared JSON; compare results are a bounded { root { leftName, rightName, comparisonResult, detailedInformation, elements[] } } tree with identical, complete and omission. A result larger than the budget is omitted whole with guidance; narrow it or re-run that operationId in its own plc_read call. get_cpu_settings (optional plcName; issue #15, not live-tested): per CPU the account locking, syslog (with its servers and the syslog attributes), system web pages, web applications, watch/force table access rules of the web server and the display, display protection, front panel display, user-defined web pages, the MultilingualSupport rows and the IP accessibility module, plus the project's PLC password policies and syslog servers; values are projected as text, uninterpreted, and a service the CPU does not offer is reported as not offered. get_cpu_settings also lists the CPU's web server users (with permissions), simple web server users and the OPC UA submodule's users (issue #13; passwords are never readable). get_umac (optional plcName; issue #12, not live-tested): the project's UMAC (engineering function rights, which make the project protected when not empty, custom and system roles with their engineering rights, project users with alias, state, session timeout, authentication type and roles, UMC users and groups, custom device function rights, the anonymous user, the password policy) and per PLC the UmacDevice's available device function rights and every role's assigned rights on it. get_cpu_certificates (optional plcName; issue #14, not live-tested; TemporaryExport): per CPU the LocalCertificateManager (EnableGlobalCertificatesStore) with every certificate of its LocalCertificateStore (Id, SubjectCommonName, ValidUntil, HasPrivateKey and, from a temporary Export(FileInfo) deleted afterwards, Sha256 over the DER bytes, Sha1Thumbprint, Subject, Issuer, NotBefore, NotAfter), the dynamic certificate management (Usage, CertificateExpirationEventActivated, RemainingCertificateLifetime, CertificateSupportedServices) and the certificates assigned through WebserverCertificate and OpcUaServerCertificate. Compare these SHA-256 fingerprints with the ones a TLS prompt lists before passing trustedCertificates; nothing here trusts a certificate. get_safety_validation (issue #25, not live-tested): the Safety Validation Assistant's activation tests with group, author, evaluation device and overall state, their safety functions (test name, description, test state, traced) and conditions, the groups and the evaluation devices. check_activation_test (testName, optional functionName, position): TestValidity.CheckValidity() of the test, function or condition (state, error count, messages); a consistency check, no test result and no acceptance. Whether CheckValidity stores a validity state is undocumented, so it is classified as a write capability: read-only refuses it.")]
    public static Task<CallToolResult> PlcRead(
        OpennessWorkerClient workerClient,
        [Description("Ordered list of PLC read operations. Each item is { operationId, operation, ...operation parameters }.")] PlcOperationRequest[] operations,
        CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
        => BatchReadTool.RunAsync(workerClient, operations, ToolName, PlcContractVersion.Current,
            PlcOperationCatalog.ValidateRead, PlcOperationCatalog.ValidateAccessMode,
            Execute(workerClient, operations, cancellationToken), RetryGuidance, cancellationToken);

    /// <summary>
    /// One executor per call, so the analysis items of the call share one evidence snapshot and its alarm workbook reads
    /// share the document budget (<see cref="PlcAlarms.PlcAlarmRequests.CallResultBudget"/>).
    /// </summary>
    private static Func<PlcOperationRequest, Task<StructuredOperationItem>> Execute(OpennessWorkerClient workerClient, IReadOnlyList<PlcOperationRequest?>? operations,
        CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        var analysis = new PlcAnalysis.PlcAnalysisSession(workerClient);
        var workbookResultChars = PlcAlarms.PlcAlarmRequests.CallResultBudget(operations);
        return async operation => PlcAddressOccupancyReader.Handles(operation.Operation)
            ? await PlcAddressOccupancyReader.ExecuteAsync(workerClient, operation, cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false)
            : PlcObjectFinder.Handles(operation.Operation)
                ? await PlcObjectFinder.ExecuteAsync(workerClient, operation, cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false)
            : PlcSdNetworkReader.Handles(operation.Operation)
                ? await PlcSdNetworkReader.ExecuteAsync(workerClient, operation, cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false)
            : PlcAnalysis.PlcAnalysisPolicy.Handles(operation.Operation)
                ? await PlcAnalysis.PlcAnalysisReader.ExecuteAsync(analysis, operation, cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false)
                : PlcPayloadContract.Project(operation,
                    await PlcWorkerInvoker.InvokeReadAsync(workerClient, operation, cancellationToken, workbookResultChars).ConfigureAwait(false));
    }

    internal static StructuredOperationBatch ApplyBudget(
        StructuredOperationBatch batch,
        int? maxItemChars = null,
        int? maxDocumentChars = null)
        => BatchReadTool.ApplyBudget(batch, ToolName, PlcContractVersion.Current,
            RetryGuidance, maxItemChars, maxDocumentChars);

    private static string RetryGuidance(StructuredOperationItem item) => item.Operation switch
    {
        "get_block_content" or "get_type_content" or Contracts.Plc.SimaticSd.SimaticSdMethods.ListNetworks =>
            "Read a smaller object or drop withDependencies, or split the batch: re-run this operationId in its own "
                + $"{ToolName} call. A single object above the limit needs the server restarted with "
                + "--max-item-chars (or TIA_MCP_MAX_ITEM_CHARS) at or above originalChars and --max-document-chars "
                + "(or TIA_MCP_MAX_DOCUMENT_CHARS) with headroom above it for the response envelope.",
        "list_tag_tables" =>
            "Narrow with plcName, folderPath or tableName (one table is the narrowest), or split the batch: "
                + $"re-run this operationId in its own {ToolName} call.",
        "list_download_targets" or "get_online_state" or "list_watch_and_force_tables" =>
            $"Narrow with plcName, or split the batch: re-run this operationId in its own {ToolName} call.",
        "get_db_values" =>
            $"Narrow with memberPath (a struct, multi-instance or array element), or split the batch: re-run this operationId in its own {ToolName} call.",
        "get_block_interface" or "get_type_interface" =>
            $"Split the batch: re-run this operationId in its own {ToolName} call; an interface above the limit needs the server restarted with --max-item-chars above originalChars.",
        PlcTagMoveMethods.ReadAddressOccupancy =>
            $"Narrow with plcName or areas, or set includeHardware false, or split the batch: re-run this operationId in its own {ToolName} call.",
        "compare_to_online" or "compare_software" or "compare_hardware" or "compare_hardware_to_online" =>
            "Lower maxElements or maxDepth, keep differencesOnly true, or split the batch: re-run this operationId in its own "
                + $"{ToolName} call.",
        "read_text_list_workbook" or "read_alarm_text_workbook" or "read_supervision_workbook" =>
            $"Lower maxElements, read one sheet with sheet and page with startRow = nextStartRow (and startColumn = nextStartColumn for a cut row), narrow with textListNames or cultures, or split the batch: re-run this operationId in its own {ToolName} call.",
        "list_text_lists" =>
            $"Narrow with plcName, or split the batch: re-run this operationId in its own {ToolName} call.",
        "read_watch_table" or "read_force_table" =>
            $"Lower maxElements, or split the batch: re-run this operationId in its own {ToolName} call.",
        "get_watch_table_content" or "get_force_table_content" =>
            $"Split the batch: re-run this operationId in its own {ToolName} call. A single table above the limit needs the server restarted with "
                + "--max-item-chars (or TIA_MCP_MAX_ITEM_CHARS) at or above originalChars.",
        PlcSourceFolderMethods.FindObjects =>
            $"Lower limit and page with offset/nextOffset, narrow with plcName or kinds, or split the batch: re-run this operationId in its own {ToolName} call.",
        PlcSourceFolderMethods.ListExternalSources or PlcSourceFolderMethods.ScanAccessibleDevices or PlcSourceFolderMethods.ReadTagComments =>
            $"Narrow with plcName (read_tag_comments: tableName or folderPath; scan_accessible_devices: lower maxElements), or split the batch: re-run this operationId in its own {ToolName} call.",
        "list_technology_objects" =>
            $"Narrow with plcName and folderPath, or split the batch: re-run this operationId in its own {ToolName} call.",
        "get_technology_object_parameters" =>
            $"Lower limit, narrow with prefix or read one parameterName, or split the batch: re-run this operationId in its own {ToolName} call.",
        "get_technology_object_content" =>
            $"Split the batch: re-run this operationId in its own {ToolName} call. A single object above the limit needs the server restarted with "
                + "--max-item-chars (or TIA_MCP_MAX_ITEM_CHARS) at or above originalChars.",
        "get_call_tree" or "find_call_paths" or "find_unused_blocks" or "find_orphaned_instance_dbs" or "analyze_change_impact" =>
            "Lower maxElements or maxDepth, or split the batch: re-run this operationId in its own "
                + $"{ToolName} call. Each result also carries a fixed evidence section of about 3,000 characters.",
        _ => $"Split the batch: re-run this operationId in its own {ToolName} call.",
    };

    internal static CallToolResult Error(string category, string message)
        => BatchReadTool.Error(ToolName, PlcContractVersion.Current, category, message);
}
